&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in sales operations, sales, strategy consulting; minimum 2+ years directly partnering with senior software/tech sales leaders ($1B+ sales orgs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in sales planning and operations including sales coverage, segmentation, territory planning, sales compensation strategy and executing a rhythm of business (MBRs, QBRs, etc).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solving, communication and interpersonal skills with ability to influence and align senior leadership and teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree or equivalent years&#39; of experience; graduate degree a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience guiding sales teams through organizational changes, shifting priorities, and evolving market strategies with minimal disruption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex sales performance and pipeline data into clear storylines, actionable recommendations, and business reviews for senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building strong partnerships across various business functions and aligning diverse cross-functional stakeholders around shared business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be remote,&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;but is not eligible to be hired in CA, CT, NJ, NY, PA, WA.&lt;/p&gt;
